{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit cap and return rules (AB 12)","requirement":"Deposits are capped at one month's rent; owners of no more than two rental properties with four units total may charge two months. A landlord must return the deposit with an itemized statement within 21 days and photograph the unit when a tenancy begins.","key_value":"one month's rent; up to two months' rent for owners of two or fewer rental properties with four residential units total","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies in California; excepted are landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC of natural persons.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC whose members are all natural persons","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Photographing the unit at the start of a tenancy is required for tenancies beginning on or after July 1, 2025; the cleaning-deduction rule applies to tenancies beginning after January 1, 2003.","coverage_quotes":["Starting July 1, 2024, landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total can charge up to two months' rent for furnished and unfurnished units if ownership is held by a natural person, family trust, or limited liability company (LLC) where all members are natural persons"]},"exemptions":"Landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, if held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC whose members are all natural persons, may charge up to two months' rent.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"AB 12","quoted_span":"Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance security deposit interest","requirement":"For units covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance, the landlord must pay interest on the tenant's security deposit at the end of each year, prorated if the tenant moves out before the year ends.","key_value":"annual interest on the security deposit; prorated at move-out","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","text":"Units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
